WEBVTT

01:10.320 --> 01:13.364
We were at the rainwater drainage station
and had a drink afterward.

01:13.448 --> 01:15.283
I didn't know he'd get drunk so quickly.

01:17.786 --> 01:19.370
You could have called a driver.

01:21.372 --> 01:22.582
You see…

01:24.042 --> 01:24.876
What?

01:26.127 --> 01:27.253
Did you leave home?

01:30.799 --> 01:32.258
Yes.

01:33.218 --> 01:34.552
It's a long story.

01:35.386 --> 01:36.888
It's a long story.

01:40.099 --> 01:42.227
What about you?
Why are you here at this hour?

01:42.852 --> 01:45.271
It's a long story for me too.

01:46.940 --> 01:49.609
Do you not want to answer me
or do you not have a choice?

01:50.276 --> 01:51.653
What about you, Director Jin?

01:53.780 --> 01:54.614
What do you mean?

01:54.697 --> 01:57.242
Normally, you'd send
a drunk colleague back home,

01:57.325 --> 01:59.077
not bring them to a motel.

02:06.000 --> 02:08.336
Past wounds are nasty.

02:09.671 --> 02:10.505
Mr. Lee.

02:13.258 --> 02:14.926
IMI MOTEL

02:15.009 --> 02:16.094
What?

02:16.678 --> 02:19.639
I thought you had left already.
Were you still here?

02:22.016 --> 02:23.935
You think you're all better now.

02:24.018 --> 02:26.104
But when you look back,
they're still infected.

02:26.187 --> 02:28.398
Now that we've met,
I hope to see you more often.

02:29.482 --> 02:30.567
Go home safely.

02:46.374 --> 02:48.459
The deeper your memories
of those wounds are,

02:49.043 --> 02:51.462
the more cowardly you become.

02:52.839 --> 02:56.134
Like air stuck in a forest of skyscrapers,

02:56.217 --> 02:58.595
you're trapped in self-pity and pain.

02:59.387 --> 03:03.057
You spin around in circles
in the same place

03:03.850 --> 03:05.935
and isolate yourself.

03:09.063 --> 03:14.694
EPISODE 6
HEAT ISLAND PHENOMENON

03:14.777 --> 03:18.114
The first heat wave warning
of this year in Seoul has been issued.

03:18.197 --> 03:21.492
Due to the heat island phenomenon
where heat is trapped,

03:21.576 --> 03:24.370
this scorching weather
will continue for some time.

03:24.454 --> 03:27.332
Roads that become hot over the day

03:27.415 --> 03:29.709
and heat from air-conditioner fans

03:29.792 --> 03:31.628
are raising the temperature even more.

03:31.711 --> 03:33.504
More from Reporter Park Cheol-min.

03:42.639 --> 03:45.475
It's steaming hot this morning.

03:46.059 --> 03:48.144
What are you doing
under the sweltering heat?

03:58.238 --> 03:59.906
Is it already that time of the year?

04:05.954 --> 04:07.538
You should stop doing this.

04:07.622 --> 04:09.415
No one eats it anyway.

04:09.499 --> 04:11.334
You're spitting. Go away.

04:11.417 --> 04:13.378
I'm worried you might get sick again.

04:37.402 --> 04:39.279
It's disaster prevention season,

04:39.362 --> 04:41.322
so he's staying at the KMA.

04:41.406 --> 04:43.283
I thought he was going to live with us.

04:43.366 --> 04:44.409
What?

04:45.952 --> 04:47.662
Yes. He was.

04:48.621 --> 04:50.290
- But…
- When is he coming back?

04:52.583 --> 04:53.668
Well…

04:55.044 --> 04:56.296
Once the rainy season ends.

05:08.683 --> 05:11.060
Damn, it's hot.

05:26.034 --> 05:27.327
Gosh.

05:32.582 --> 05:35.585
Goodness, I wonder
how hot it'll get today.

05:36.836 --> 05:38.004
Hello.

05:44.802 --> 05:46.971
Since an anticyclone is over Korea,

05:47.055 --> 05:48.389
- a lot of sunlight
- I'm sorry.

05:48.473 --> 05:50.308
and heat are moving into the country.

05:57.231 --> 05:58.816
Although temporary,

05:58.900 --> 06:02.111
the temperature in June
is rising higher than average.

06:02.612 --> 06:04.447
You're here early.

06:04.530 --> 06:05.406
Sorry?

06:05.490 --> 06:08.242
Isn't Chief Team Two
on night duty starting today?

06:08.868 --> 06:09.744
Starting today?

06:10.661 --> 06:11.662
Right.

06:11.746 --> 06:14.373
Your recent move
from Gangwon Office must've confused you.

06:15.416 --> 06:17.085
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

07:13.224 --> 07:15.351
Butter.

07:16.936 --> 07:18.688
Butter.

07:24.360 --> 07:25.695
The smell.

07:38.040 --> 07:42.628
INCOMING CALL
APARTMENT 1302

07:48.050 --> 07:50.344
CALLING
APARTMENT 1201

08:21.501 --> 08:22.585
Yes?

08:24.003 --> 08:26.172
- Oh, you were home.
- Yes.

08:26.255 --> 08:27.757
How may I help you?

08:27.840 --> 08:30.301
We texted you several times,

08:30.384 --> 08:31.969
but you didn't reply.

08:32.053 --> 08:34.555
A new trainee will come here soon,

08:34.639 --> 08:36.641
so we'd like you to move out.

08:36.724 --> 08:38.476
By next week, if possible.

08:39.644 --> 08:40.770
By next week?

08:41.437 --> 08:42.897
The room needs maintenance

08:42.980 --> 08:45.066
before we welcome a new trainee.

08:45.149 --> 08:47.652
You can only stay here for a month anyway.

08:47.735 --> 08:49.111
I'm sure you knew that.

08:49.195 --> 08:50.404
Right.

08:50.488 --> 08:52.281
Please move out by next week.

08:52.365 --> 08:53.991
- Goodbye.
- Okay.

09:27.567 --> 09:29.277
You ran even in this weather?

09:30.069 --> 09:32.780
Do you not sleep in
even when you're working nighttime?

09:35.449 --> 09:36.659
What's good here?

09:38.619 --> 09:40.079
Let's reconsider this.

09:41.622 --> 09:42.873
Reconsider what?

09:43.624 --> 09:44.625
You and me.

09:47.503 --> 09:49.046
"Just as a loud noise is created

09:49.839 --> 09:51.799
when a cloud meets another cloud,

09:51.882 --> 09:55.511
I wish I could be bold enough
to shout unconsciously

09:55.595 --> 09:59.265
in this relationship I have with you."

10:00.641 --> 10:03.185
"Just as a bright light appears

10:03.269 --> 10:05.730
when a cloud suddenly meets another cloud,

10:05.813 --> 10:07.607
I wish being with you

10:08.149 --> 10:10.776
could shed light on the path
I have wandered away from."

10:12.194 --> 10:14.071
By the way, what do you think this means?

10:14.989 --> 10:16.115
This last part.

10:16.866 --> 10:19.243
"You shine brightly when you tell me

10:19.327 --> 10:22.371
that rain needs to meet another rain
for them to get drenched."

10:25.708 --> 10:30.004
"Our similarities help us
understand each other's hearts."

10:31.380 --> 10:32.798
Maybe that's what it means.

10:33.674 --> 10:34.884
Give me an example.

10:38.429 --> 10:39.555
Something like this.

10:39.639 --> 10:41.766
- Come on.
- What?

10:41.849 --> 10:43.768
- What was that?
- Back then, I didn't know

10:44.435 --> 10:47.730
- What?
- how much pain we'd have to endure

10:47.813 --> 10:50.775
to understand the beautiful phrase,

10:50.858 --> 10:54.153
"Rain needs to meet
another rain for it to get drenched."

10:55.988 --> 10:57.323
Why suddenly?

11:01.744 --> 11:04.705
I thought it would be okay,
but I guess I was wrong.

11:08.668 --> 11:11.003
My mind has been racing

11:11.087 --> 11:13.339
ever since I saw you
yesterday at the motel.

11:14.090 --> 11:16.342
My past trauma keeps resurfacing,

11:16.926 --> 11:18.094
and I get upset.

11:20.096 --> 11:22.264
That woman has nothing to do with me.

11:23.224 --> 11:26.727
I want to believe that and move on.

11:27.353 --> 11:30.606
But I'm still trapped at that moment.

11:33.984 --> 11:36.779
I know that you're not lying to me.

11:36.862 --> 11:39.156
That's why it's an even bigger problem.

11:39.824 --> 11:41.992
It's clear you're telling me the truth,

11:42.701 --> 11:44.495
but I still can't trust you.

11:47.331 --> 11:48.290
Director Jin.

11:48.374 --> 11:50.167
Let's take some time to think this over.

11:51.919 --> 11:55.297
I'm not doing this for you.
I'm doing this for me.

12:01.762 --> 12:03.347
I'll go first. Enjoy your food.

12:06.934 --> 12:08.060
It was my father.

12:11.522 --> 12:13.357
I went to the motel last night…

12:15.818 --> 12:17.570
because of him.

12:25.828 --> 12:26.704
Mr. Lee Si-woo?

12:27.496 --> 12:29.331
I'm here to see Mr. Lee Myung-han.

12:34.336 --> 12:35.504
Come in.

12:37.673 --> 12:40.676
Hey, why don't you just fold?

12:40.759 --> 12:42.470
What's taking you so long?

12:44.805 --> 12:46.515
- Damn it.
- Myung-han.

12:46.599 --> 12:48.559
- Your son is here.
- Here you go.

12:48.642 --> 12:50.978
- You got a high score.
- He's one handsome man.

12:51.061 --> 12:53.647
- Si-woo. You're here.
- What was that?

12:54.940 --> 12:56.192
Come…

12:56.275 --> 12:57.818
Hey, Si-woo!

12:57.902 --> 12:59.278
Si-woo…

12:59.862 --> 13:01.822
Damn it. Si-woo!

13:01.906 --> 13:03.365
Hey!

13:03.449 --> 13:05.284
Hey, wait!

13:05.367 --> 13:07.286
Come on, Si-woo.

13:08.454 --> 13:10.039
You punk.

13:10.122 --> 13:11.957
How could you just leave like that?

13:12.041 --> 13:13.167
You're gambling again?

13:13.250 --> 13:15.753
Is this why
you've been blowing up my phone?

13:16.712 --> 13:19.548
I had no choice.
You're the only son I have.

13:19.632 --> 13:21.967
First, give me the money you brought.

13:24.970 --> 13:26.013
What's going on?

13:26.096 --> 13:27.306
Damn it.

13:27.389 --> 13:29.433
- Did you not bring it?
- I don't have…

13:30.392 --> 13:32.728
- any money.
- Why don't you?

13:32.811 --> 13:34.355
I'm very well aware

13:34.438 --> 13:37.191
that you landed a nice job
and get paid every month.

13:37.274 --> 13:39.151
Last year,

13:39.235 --> 13:41.320
you took all my savings.

13:42.321 --> 13:43.155
Did I?

13:44.156 --> 13:46.742
I'm fine with coins too,
so give me all you have.

13:47.451 --> 13:50.329
I'm about to lose everything and die here.

13:50.412 --> 13:51.247
Okay?

13:51.330 --> 13:53.290
- Hurry.
- I said I had no money!

13:53.374 --> 13:56.043
I'm staying at the training center
because I have no money for a deposit!

13:56.126 --> 13:57.419
Can't you take out a loan?

13:58.337 --> 14:01.757
Don't civil servants
receive loan benefits?

14:03.968 --> 14:05.594
Don't ever call me again.

14:05.678 --> 14:07.263
If you do,

14:07.346 --> 14:09.431
I'll report you to the police.

14:10.307 --> 14:11.892
You bastard.

14:11.976 --> 14:14.103
Hey, stop right there.

14:14.186 --> 14:15.896
You little… Hey.

14:16.981 --> 14:18.107
Gosh.

14:18.732 --> 14:20.109
Damn it.

14:23.654 --> 14:24.822
What about you?

14:25.573 --> 14:27.199
Why are you here at this hour?

14:28.450 --> 14:31.328
It's a long story for me too.

14:32.872 --> 14:35.833
Do you not want to answer me
or do you not have a choice?

14:36.584 --> 14:38.168
What about you, Director Jin?

14:40.337 --> 14:41.589
"Director Jin"?

14:43.841 --> 14:44.925
What do you mean?

14:45.634 --> 14:47.970
Normally, you'd send
a drunk colleague back home,

14:48.637 --> 14:51.015
not bring them to a motel.

16:29.947 --> 16:31.281
The community service center?

16:32.116 --> 16:33.033
Why?

16:34.451 --> 16:35.619
To register our marriage.

16:36.453 --> 16:38.622
We need to give them
our marriage certificate

16:38.706 --> 16:41.458
to get the housing loan for newlyweds.

16:42.376 --> 16:43.544
Really?

16:44.420 --> 16:46.839
What about a contract extension
for our current house?

16:46.922 --> 16:49.216
It's too expensive,
and there are no benefits.

16:56.015 --> 16:57.641
Why the long face?

16:59.893 --> 17:01.061
Don't tell me…

17:03.439 --> 17:05.190
that house has already grown on you.

17:06.608 --> 17:07.568
It has.

17:08.235 --> 17:09.945
Oh, dear.

17:11.363 --> 17:12.740
Yu-jin.

17:13.574 --> 17:14.742
Home is anywhere

17:14.825 --> 17:17.995
we settle down and grow fond of.

17:18.829 --> 17:21.331
I'll look for a nice place,
so don't you worry.

17:21.415 --> 17:22.458
Okay?

17:23.375 --> 17:26.962
Right. I'll give you
my seal and identification card.

17:27.046 --> 17:28.630
Can you register it for me?

17:29.339 --> 17:30.758
I'd love to come with you,

17:30.841 --> 17:32.801
but my column is due tomorrow.

17:32.885 --> 17:35.054
- Will that be okay with you?
- Of course.

17:35.137 --> 17:36.221
Great.

17:41.351 --> 17:42.895
- Do you want mine?
- What?

17:44.146 --> 17:45.606
You barely ate any.

17:45.689 --> 17:47.274
Do you not like chicken?

17:50.027 --> 17:52.696
Gosh. You even left a drumstick.

18:03.499 --> 18:05.375
- Did you have lunch?
- Yes, sir.

18:06.627 --> 18:08.087
- Did you?
- Yes, sir.

18:09.046 --> 18:11.673
I had a bit of work to do,
so I just had gimbap.

18:11.757 --> 18:15.552
Goodness. You should still eat properly.

18:15.636 --> 18:18.138
- Your well-being comes before work.
- Right.

18:18.722 --> 18:21.225
- By the way, what are you working on?
- Sorry?

18:21.308 --> 18:22.226
It's nothing.

18:22.309 --> 18:23.602
What is it?

18:24.561 --> 18:25.813
To be honest,

18:25.896 --> 18:27.773
the director asked me to write a column.

18:28.357 --> 18:30.025
A column? What kind?

18:31.276 --> 18:33.195
- A themed story.
- Themed…

18:34.905 --> 18:37.282
He told you to write that?

18:38.742 --> 18:40.786
Yes, I did.

18:40.869 --> 18:42.788
But that's my job.

18:42.871 --> 18:45.541
We need to send our paper
to the printing office soon,

18:45.624 --> 18:47.042
but you haven't finished yet.

18:47.626 --> 18:49.920
I can't just sit still
and wait until you finish.

18:50.504 --> 18:53.048
I'm just adding
the finishing touches right now.

18:53.632 --> 18:55.634
I'm pretty much done.

18:55.717 --> 18:58.178
Then finish it and hand it over.

18:58.262 --> 18:59.388
What about him?

18:59.471 --> 19:01.473
You can write yours too.

19:02.099 --> 19:03.600
Both of you can write one.

19:03.684 --> 19:06.478
I'll choose the better one. Okay?

19:09.273 --> 19:11.275
Assistant Director Kim, good luck.

19:13.318 --> 19:14.736
You too.

19:14.820 --> 19:16.155
- Thank you.
- Let's do this.

19:18.615 --> 19:20.784
- Deputy Director Han, good luck.
- What?

19:20.868 --> 19:23.328
Thanks. You too.

19:29.084 --> 19:30.377
Fine.

19:31.920 --> 19:35.591
I'll finish it. I'll finish it for sure.

19:36.258 --> 19:39.011
I'll make sure to finish it.

19:46.101 --> 19:49.188
MARRIAGE CERTIFICATE

19:49.271 --> 19:52.191
WIFE
SEAL OR SIGNATURE

20:15.714 --> 20:17.799
- Goodbye.
- Goodbye.

20:25.140 --> 20:26.058
Done.

20:27.643 --> 20:29.186
- Already?
- Yes.

20:29.937 --> 20:31.271
Oh, are you not done yet?

20:31.980 --> 20:33.023
Well…

20:33.523 --> 20:37.027
I still have other work to do.

20:37.611 --> 20:39.279
It's endless.

20:40.656 --> 20:42.241
Don't worry about me. Go first.

20:42.324 --> 20:43.325
Yes, sir.

20:47.329 --> 20:49.539
Okay, then. See you tomorrow.

20:49.623 --> 20:50.707
Bye.

20:51.625 --> 20:52.834
Good work today.

21:01.385 --> 21:02.594
Damn it.

21:14.231 --> 21:15.732
You're here early.

21:15.816 --> 21:18.360
I forgot that we were
on night duty starting today

21:18.443 --> 21:20.237
and came 12 hours early.

21:20.320 --> 21:23.282
I thought I was late this morning,
so I rushed over here.

21:23.365 --> 21:25.284
But Chief Team One was having a meeting.

21:25.367 --> 21:27.661
How could you always
be tardy to our meetings,

21:27.744 --> 21:29.121
but not theirs?

21:31.498 --> 21:34.626
You should have just gone home
last night when I got drunk.

21:34.710 --> 21:36.169
I must have been a lousy drunk.

21:36.253 --> 21:38.005
It's disaster prevention season.

21:38.088 --> 21:40.716
We're so busy,
we need all the help we can get.

21:40.799 --> 21:42.884
I can't afford to lose
a crucial member to the streets.

21:43.927 --> 21:46.138
Don't make me laugh. I'm only a burden.

21:47.097 --> 21:49.766
- Did you have dinner?
- Not yet. I'm not hungry.

21:49.850 --> 21:52.436
I'll give you 30 minutes.
Go grab something to eat.

21:53.437 --> 21:54.604
Okay.

21:59.609 --> 22:00.694
Gosh.

22:01.737 --> 22:02.696
Hey.

22:06.199 --> 22:07.326
What's wrong?

22:14.666 --> 22:16.543
Why was he glaring at me?

22:19.296 --> 22:21.131
- Hello.
- Hello.

22:27.346 --> 22:28.680
This is…

22:29.765 --> 22:31.767
Hey, I had dinner.

22:36.563 --> 22:38.231
Didn't we confirm this already?

22:40.942 --> 22:42.277
This is bad.

22:42.360 --> 22:44.571
The temperature is high,
and so is the radiation.

22:44.654 --> 22:48.033
The sun will set soon,
but the temperature is still 28°C.

22:48.658 --> 22:51.369
Seoul is going to melt
due to the heat island phenomenon.

22:52.162 --> 22:54.414
Do you think
the atmospheric flow will change?

22:54.498 --> 22:58.043
Who knows?
Maybe we'll get a sudden rain shower.

23:13.850 --> 23:16.103
Call me. Mom is really sick.

23:38.250 --> 23:41.044
How could she not call
when I said you were sick?

23:41.128 --> 23:42.671
Just let her be.

23:43.588 --> 23:46.007
She's on night duty starting today.

23:46.091 --> 23:49.344
Still, she should at least text
and ask how you're doing.

23:49.427 --> 23:53.056
We must have been too lenient on her,
seeing how impudent she's become.

23:53.932 --> 23:56.393
She probably thinks
we're trying to fool her

23:57.060 --> 24:00.230
and make her come home
by saying that I'm sick.

24:04.901 --> 24:05.819
TAE-KYUNG

24:07.571 --> 24:09.781
What's the probability
of a rain shower at dawn?

24:11.283 --> 24:14.161
Gosh. Are you serious?

24:18.832 --> 24:21.835
SUPPLEMENTARY WEATHER CHART

24:32.512 --> 24:35.098
It's pretty quiet today.

24:35.182 --> 24:36.433
It can't always be noisy.

24:37.267 --> 24:40.645
There could be localized heavy rain,
so please monitor it.

24:41.354 --> 24:42.606
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

25:11.343 --> 25:13.220
Is something going on?

25:16.139 --> 25:16.973
What?

25:17.557 --> 25:18.808
Did you say something?

25:19.726 --> 25:22.020
Something seems to be on your mind.

25:22.103 --> 25:23.021
Well…

25:23.772 --> 25:26.733
It's just a family matter.

25:34.532 --> 25:35.742
Honey.

25:37.494 --> 25:41.456
Can I take the Grade Five
technical exam again?

25:55.679 --> 25:57.097
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

26:02.435 --> 26:04.062
- Director Jin.
- Yes?

26:04.145 --> 26:05.563
Should I answer it instead?

26:05.647 --> 26:06.773
No, it's okay.

26:08.024 --> 26:10.318
Jin Ha-kyung of Chief Team Two speaking.

26:13.238 --> 26:14.281
Sorry?

26:14.364 --> 26:17.075
You have a guest.

26:17.701 --> 26:21.037
He keeps insisting on seeing you.

26:21.538 --> 26:22.706
Yes, ma'am.

26:22.789 --> 26:24.666
Let me.

26:25.417 --> 26:26.835
Hello, Director Jin.

26:27.335 --> 26:29.713
My name is Lee Myung-han.

26:29.796 --> 26:31.715
I'm Lee Si-woo's father.

26:37.637 --> 26:39.055
I have something urgent

26:39.139 --> 26:42.517
to tell you about my son.

26:42.600 --> 26:43.518
Do you think

26:44.519 --> 26:47.272
you could spare me ten minutes?

26:48.523 --> 26:49.649
Sure.

27:10.670 --> 27:13.882
This brat still hasn't called.

27:38.865 --> 27:40.116
Darn it.

27:55.423 --> 27:57.425
No.

27:57.509 --> 27:58.968
I shouldn't.

28:11.356 --> 28:13.858
No, you crazy bastard. What should I do?

28:28.289 --> 28:29.999
Are you Mr. Lee Si-woo's father?

28:30.959 --> 28:32.127
Yes, I am.

28:32.961 --> 28:34.003
I'm his father.

28:34.712 --> 28:36.464
I see. Hello.

28:38.383 --> 28:40.385
So how can I help you?

28:45.014 --> 28:48.560
To be honest,
I have something urgent to tell you.

28:52.230 --> 28:55.984
Goodness. I feel bad
about saying this to a stranger.

28:57.444 --> 28:58.903
But then again,

28:58.987 --> 29:01.364
you two seem to have something special.

29:04.075 --> 29:05.368
What do you mean?

29:05.452 --> 29:08.329
I'm well aware
that you guys are close enough

29:09.247 --> 29:11.958
to go to motels together.

29:17.046 --> 29:17.922
I see.

29:18.006 --> 29:20.091
Your colleagues don't know, do they?

29:21.551 --> 29:22.969
I get it.

29:23.052 --> 29:25.138
I won't talk too loudly.

29:26.097 --> 29:27.223
Okay.

29:27.932 --> 29:31.060
Anyway, so it's true that you two

29:31.144 --> 29:32.854
are in a relationship, right?

29:37.275 --> 29:40.111
I saw you two at a motel last night too.

29:49.287 --> 29:51.581
I'm sorry, but why did you want to see me?

29:51.664 --> 29:52.874
Do you have any money?

29:54.834 --> 29:57.504
You seem to have a lot of work experience

29:57.587 --> 29:59.297
and seem to be older than him.

29:59.380 --> 30:01.424
Plus, you're a director.

30:01.508 --> 30:05.887
That must mean
you get paid more than he does.

30:05.970 --> 30:07.597
You see,

30:08.181 --> 30:10.975
I'm in dire need of money.

30:11.059 --> 30:13.436
Do you think you could lend me some?

30:33.373 --> 30:34.499
Hey.

30:34.582 --> 30:36.251
Where's Director Jin?

30:36.793 --> 30:39.420
- She left after taking a call.
- Beats me.

30:41.840 --> 30:43.883
- Try calling her.
- Okay.

30:56.604 --> 30:58.940
TAE-KYUNG

31:06.406 --> 31:08.825
This is Director Jin Ha-kyung's phone.

31:10.869 --> 31:11.703
Sorry?

31:31.180 --> 31:33.725
- Ma'am, please come with us.
- Okay.

31:35.143 --> 31:37.312
911 EMERGENCY
AMBULANCE

31:42.525 --> 31:44.777
Shouldn't we tell Director Jin to go home?

31:45.695 --> 31:48.406
She's not the type who'd listen to us.

31:52.452 --> 31:53.995
What should we do, Senior Forecaster Um?

32:21.648 --> 32:22.774
Director Jin.

32:25.360 --> 32:27.278
Your sister just called.

32:28.363 --> 32:29.739
Your mother is very sick.

32:30.323 --> 32:31.407
Here.

32:36.329 --> 32:37.413
Director Jin!

32:38.498 --> 32:39.499
Right.

32:39.999 --> 32:41.542
Don't worry about my mom.

32:41.626 --> 32:44.796
She sometimes says that
when we get into an argument.

32:45.463 --> 32:47.632
- Let's go.
- She's going to the emergency room.

32:48.549 --> 32:49.509
What?

32:49.592 --> 32:52.345
Your mother.
They even called an ambulance.

32:53.304 --> 32:55.515
It seems pretty serious.

32:58.851 --> 33:01.104
Jin Ha-kyung. How could you do this?

33:01.604 --> 33:03.398
Mom is sick.

33:03.481 --> 33:05.775
I know you're mad at her,

33:05.858 --> 33:07.360
but how could you be this cold?

33:07.443 --> 33:10.571
Shouldn't you have
at least called to check on her?

33:16.911 --> 33:20.999
She's dying right now.

33:25.294 --> 33:27.422
- Which hospital are you headed to?
- I don't know.

33:27.505 --> 33:29.340
They're taking us
to the closest emergency room.

33:29.424 --> 33:30.466
I'll call you.

33:30.550 --> 33:33.052
Okay. I'll go there once my shift is--

33:33.136 --> 33:36.014
Hey! I said Mom is dying!

33:36.723 --> 33:39.809
- You know I can't leave right now.
- Come here!

33:39.892 --> 33:40.935
Right now!

33:41.019 --> 33:44.272
I said I got it.
I'll go once the morning team--

33:44.355 --> 33:47.316
Unbelievable. Forget it! I'm hanging up!

33:51.779 --> 33:52.613
Director Jin.

33:54.866 --> 33:56.534
I'm okay. You can go in first.

33:59.245 --> 34:00.288
Director Jin.

34:02.540 --> 34:03.750
Gosh.

34:05.334 --> 34:08.129
Currently, due to the anticyclone,

34:08.212 --> 34:10.757
the atmosphere
will remain the same until tomorrow.

34:10.840 --> 34:12.592
It'll be a hot night
due to the heat island phenomenon.

34:12.675 --> 34:14.052
It'll be even hotter during the day.

34:14.135 --> 34:18.014
Anyway, the situation will remain
the same until tomorrow morning.

34:18.598 --> 34:19.724
So go to your mom.

34:22.477 --> 34:24.145
I'll be on the lookout.

34:30.526 --> 34:31.986
Do you not trust me?

34:33.571 --> 34:37.033
You trust us to do
the work you assign us, don't you?

34:38.659 --> 34:40.495
I do trust you.

34:40.578 --> 34:43.831
This is my responsibility.
I need to oversee my team.

34:43.915 --> 34:47.251
Everyone in this building
knows how responsible you are.

34:47.335 --> 34:50.505
Right now, you need to fulfill
your responsibilities as a daughter.

34:54.926 --> 34:56.844
Let me make it up to you, Ha-kyung.

35:03.267 --> 35:04.393
Go on.

35:07.563 --> 35:09.732
Do call me if something happens.

35:16.781 --> 35:18.032
Forecaster Lee.

35:18.783 --> 35:19.951
Come on.

35:20.034 --> 35:21.619
Coming, sir.

35:42.431 --> 35:44.016
What happened to her?

35:46.894 --> 35:48.020
I don't know.

35:48.104 --> 35:49.981
They drew her blood and took an X-ray.

35:51.190 --> 35:53.568
She felt sluggish and lied down,

35:53.651 --> 35:55.153
then she felt dizzy.

35:56.320 --> 35:57.989
She even threw up all her food.

35:58.072 --> 36:00.366
And when she got up to go to the bathroom,

36:01.868 --> 36:05.163
she became unsteady and fell.

36:07.665 --> 36:11.460
Seriously. She was bleeding profusely
from her forehead.

36:12.420 --> 36:16.632
I thought she'd die right there, you brat.

36:22.889 --> 36:24.056
And the test results?

36:25.933 --> 36:27.602
It's going to take some time.

36:27.685 --> 36:31.314
They have too many emergency patients,
so they're behind on the tests.

36:51.667 --> 36:52.627
Senior Forecaster Um.

36:52.710 --> 36:54.712
- You asked for this.
- Thanks.

36:55.379 --> 36:58.049
Please check Seoul's
ground-surface temperature

36:58.132 --> 36:59.884
and solar radiation level
every ten minutes.

36:59.967 --> 37:01.052
Yes, sir.

37:02.261 --> 37:04.305
Are you checking
the movement of the anticyclone?

37:04.388 --> 37:08.059
I am. I don't think
it will change drastically anytime soon.

37:08.142 --> 37:10.311
Okay. Let me know if the speed increases.

37:10.394 --> 37:11.395
Yes, sir.

37:26.369 --> 37:29.622
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

37:39.674 --> 37:40.883
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

37:40.967 --> 37:42.593
DID YOU…

37:51.269 --> 37:53.020
Did you arrive at the hospital?

38:13.291 --> 38:15.167
What can I do?

38:16.043 --> 38:17.420
What should I do?

38:17.503 --> 38:19.005
Damn it. What time is it?

38:29.140 --> 38:29.974
Jin…

38:31.142 --> 38:32.685
JIN HA-KYUNG

38:38.399 --> 38:40.109
No, I can't. This isn't right.

38:45.072 --> 38:46.282
Damn it!

38:50.745 --> 38:52.038
What time is it?

39:01.756 --> 39:04.925
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

39:05.009 --> 39:06.886
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

39:06.969 --> 39:09.138
- Hello.
- Hello.

39:09.764 --> 39:11.140
- Hello.
- Hello.

39:11.223 --> 39:13.517
- Hello.
- Good morning.

39:31.952 --> 39:33.496
Come on.

39:33.579 --> 39:35.790
Where is she? Why isn't she there?

39:38.084 --> 39:39.168
Damn it.

39:44.924 --> 39:45.925
Good work.

39:46.008 --> 39:47.218
Why are you…

39:47.301 --> 39:48.469
Goodness.

39:48.552 --> 39:50.304
Did you spend the night here?

39:50.388 --> 39:52.348
Yes. I was busy working.

39:54.016 --> 39:56.477
By the way, I don't see Director Jin.

39:56.560 --> 39:57.770
Where is she?

39:57.853 --> 39:59.730
She left first due to personal reasons.

39:59.814 --> 40:01.273
I see.

40:01.357 --> 40:04.318
Why are you looking for her
this early in the morning?

40:05.111 --> 40:07.863
It's nothing serious,
so don't worry about it.

40:09.156 --> 40:11.700
- Should we have some hangover soup?
- Sure.

40:11.784 --> 40:12.910
- Hey.
- That'd be great.

40:12.993 --> 40:14.203
- I'd love that.
- Let's go.

40:14.286 --> 40:15.246
Enjoy your meal.

40:15.329 --> 40:16.705
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

40:23.087 --> 40:25.089
This is driving me crazy.
What should I do?

40:26.298 --> 40:28.926
Why does he come
to our department so often these days?

40:29.009 --> 40:30.094
I know, right?

40:30.177 --> 40:33.139
It's as if he forgot
how mercilessly he dumped Director Jin.

40:33.222 --> 40:34.974
I see him all the time.

40:35.057 --> 40:37.226
He just needs her help. That's all.

40:37.309 --> 40:38.394
Help with what?

40:38.477 --> 40:40.312
- His column.
- His column?

40:40.396 --> 40:43.023
Are you talking about that themed story?

40:43.107 --> 40:46.360
Yes. She had helped him
with every single one of them.

40:46.444 --> 40:48.487
What? No way.

40:48.571 --> 40:50.573
I'm sure some already knew about it.

40:50.656 --> 40:52.366
Didn't you, Assistant Director Shin?

40:53.200 --> 40:54.535
See?

40:54.618 --> 40:57.872
Gosh, no way. What a jerk.

40:57.955 --> 41:02.168
If you think about it,
Director Jin is a bit soft.

41:02.710 --> 41:04.170
Right, Assistant Director Shin?

41:07.131 --> 41:08.257
Doors opening.

41:11.093 --> 41:12.595
I should go home.

41:12.678 --> 41:14.263
Why? You're not eating?

41:14.346 --> 41:16.640
No, I'm not hungry.
I'll see you later tonight.

41:16.724 --> 41:18.309
- Okay. Bye.
- Okay.

41:19.560 --> 41:21.604
How about dried pollack
instead of ox head?

41:21.687 --> 41:23.647
- Sure.
- I'm excited.

41:23.731 --> 41:26.025
Didn't I ask for all
the past commemorative speech scripts

41:26.108 --> 41:27.776
for World Meteorological Day?

41:27.860 --> 41:29.695
Who told you to summarize them?

41:29.778 --> 41:32.114
The details of
the Administrator's speech aren't related

41:32.198 --> 41:34.533
to the basic planning
of the event which is our job.

41:34.617 --> 41:36.327
Who told you to make that decision?

41:36.410 --> 41:38.078
I'm the director here.

41:38.913 --> 41:39.747
I'm sorry, sir.

41:39.830 --> 41:42.458
You always make mistakes.

41:43.709 --> 41:45.127
Prepare them again.

42:00.518 --> 42:01.644
Assistant Director Shin.

42:19.119 --> 42:20.204
Here.

42:21.539 --> 42:22.373
What about breakfast?

42:22.456 --> 42:25.709
The kids and I had the soup you made.

42:25.793 --> 42:27.336
I see. Did they go to school?

42:27.419 --> 42:28.671
Of course.

42:32.299 --> 42:34.552
Our eldest wants to take art classes.

42:35.886 --> 42:39.014
English, math, taekwondo, and art?

42:39.098 --> 42:40.224
Goodness.

42:41.392 --> 42:43.435
That's almost 800,000
to 900,000 won per month.

42:46.063 --> 42:47.898
We'll have to do the same
for our younger one.

42:49.024 --> 42:51.110
Yes. I know.

42:57.658 --> 42:59.201
Will one year be enough?

43:01.120 --> 43:03.622
I can't hold out for more than that.

43:04.665 --> 43:05.833
Myung-ju.

43:07.626 --> 43:09.795
Promise me you'll come back
in a year without regrets

43:09.878 --> 43:11.964
even if you don't pass the exam.

43:12.631 --> 43:14.049
If you can promise me that,

43:14.133 --> 43:16.010
I'll try my best to stay strong.

43:24.518 --> 43:25.769
You're so lucky

43:26.562 --> 43:28.272
to have a wife like me.

43:30.691 --> 43:32.318
Of course.

43:32.901 --> 43:34.445
I'm one lucky man.

43:38.741 --> 43:40.618
Thank you, Honey.

43:41.619 --> 43:43.454
I promise I'll pass.

43:48.584 --> 43:49.585
Goodness.

43:51.503 --> 43:53.339
This is bad.

43:53.922 --> 43:55.758
You cry more easily now.

43:57.509 --> 43:58.677
Gosh.

44:02.473 --> 44:04.391
This coffee is good.

44:49.228 --> 44:51.105
She's extremely dehydrated.

44:51.188 --> 44:54.274
Her hemoglobin levels are low

44:54.358 --> 44:56.527
as well as her electrolyte levels.

44:57.861 --> 45:01.532
For now, we've administered some fluids
and prescribed her some medicine.

45:01.615 --> 45:03.867
She'll be better once she's done.

45:04.660 --> 45:06.995
Does she not have to be hospitalized?

45:07.079 --> 45:08.580
She can go home.

45:08.664 --> 45:11.208
She needs to eat and rest well.

45:12.000 --> 45:14.378
Most of all, she shouldn't get stressed.

45:14.461 --> 45:16.380
So do your best to please her.

45:16.463 --> 45:18.507
Please relay this message
to your sister too.

45:19.508 --> 45:21.051
Okay. Thank you.

45:28.100 --> 45:30.936
She's dehydrated.
She just needs some rest.

45:31.019 --> 45:34.148
- What can we do?
- We need to treat her well.

45:34.231 --> 45:35.107
You should.

45:37.985 --> 45:40.028
- Don't point fingers.
- You could do better.

45:40.112 --> 45:41.071
What did I do?

45:41.780 --> 45:44.074
- I didn't want to upset her.
- We're at a hospital.

45:44.158 --> 45:45.492
Be quiet.

45:49.580 --> 45:51.915
- Be quiet.
- Mom's smiling.

46:02.009 --> 46:05.804
MOTEL

46:16.690 --> 46:18.525
This is ten million won.

46:18.609 --> 46:21.069
This is my entire savings.

46:21.653 --> 46:23.071
This is really the last time.

46:26.158 --> 46:27.784
I knew it.

46:28.494 --> 46:32.206
Your girlfriend has more power
over you than I do.

46:32.998 --> 46:34.208
Right?

46:34.291 --> 46:37.377
Director Jin is your girlfriend, right?

46:39.004 --> 46:41.215
She looked a bit old,

46:41.298 --> 46:43.091
but she was pretty.

46:43.175 --> 46:45.677
She looked graceful and classy.

46:45.761 --> 46:50.390
By the way,
how high of a rank is a director?

46:50.474 --> 46:52.267
Her salary must be high.

46:52.351 --> 46:53.894
You little punk.

46:53.977 --> 46:56.605
You take after me. You're good with women.

46:56.688 --> 46:58.440
Right? You punk.

46:59.107 --> 47:02.319
Don't tell me you met Director Jin.

47:06.615 --> 47:08.575
Aren't you here because she talked to you?

47:11.370 --> 47:12.788
Do you have any money?

47:12.871 --> 47:16.750
You see, I'm in dire need of money.

47:16.833 --> 47:18.877
Do you think you could lend me some?

47:20.837 --> 47:25.050
I love everything about my son

47:25.133 --> 47:27.761
but he's not exactly loaded.

47:28.929 --> 47:32.099
But seeing how
he's working at Headquarters,

47:32.182 --> 47:34.518
he must be competent.

47:38.689 --> 47:41.191
You should make an investment

47:41.275 --> 47:43.318
if you want to date a young guy.

47:44.069 --> 47:45.946
Ten million won would be enough.

47:52.077 --> 47:53.829
You're crazy.

47:53.912 --> 47:55.998
Everything's fine.

47:56.498 --> 47:58.875
Hey. From the way I see it,

47:58.959 --> 48:01.295
she's head over heels for you.

48:01.378 --> 48:04.631
She looks more stable
and considerate compared

48:04.715 --> 48:06.425
to that reporter chick you dated.

48:06.508 --> 48:08.010
But most of all,

48:08.093 --> 48:09.970
her looks are totally my type.

48:10.679 --> 48:13.557
Anyway, thanks. Use this for a cab.

48:13.640 --> 48:14.766
What the…

48:16.977 --> 48:19.563
You bastard. How dare you grab
your father by the collar?

48:19.646 --> 48:20.731
Let go!

48:20.814 --> 48:22.399
Why are you doing this to me?

48:22.482 --> 48:25.027
- What did I do?
- Can you please…

48:26.111 --> 48:27.821
let me live?

48:29.156 --> 48:30.407
I beg you.

48:31.408 --> 48:33.827
Please stop muscling in on my life.

48:34.453 --> 48:35.829
Please.

48:46.715 --> 48:49.343
That punk.

49:01.146 --> 49:03.732
DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

49:11.823 --> 49:13.116
Come here, Mom.

49:15.369 --> 49:16.495
Goodness.

49:21.375 --> 49:23.085
Eat before you go.

49:23.168 --> 49:24.503
Just rest.

49:24.586 --> 49:26.588
I made some young radish kimchi.

49:26.672 --> 49:30.050
I told Tae-kyung
to give you some side dishes.

49:30.133 --> 49:31.510
Did you get to try them?

49:34.388 --> 49:35.639
What?

49:35.722 --> 49:36.973
The guy upstairs didn't give them?

49:37.557 --> 49:38.600
Guy upstairs?

49:38.684 --> 49:41.520
I mean, you changed your passcode
and didn't pick up either.

49:41.603 --> 49:43.480
You should have left it with the guard.

49:44.231 --> 49:45.107
I…

49:45.190 --> 49:48.360
I didn't want them to go bad.
There was bulgogi too.

49:48.443 --> 49:50.821
Enough. Be quiet.

49:50.904 --> 49:53.907
Go get me a glass of water. Goodness.

50:01.206 --> 50:02.624
What a strange guy.

50:02.708 --> 50:05.001
Why hasn't he given them to her yet?

50:06.545 --> 50:07.713
He seemed to be living alone.

50:08.463 --> 50:09.506
Hold on.

50:09.589 --> 50:11.299
Did he eat them all?

50:16.012 --> 50:18.807
DOES IT SMELL?
NATURAL MINERAL PRESERVATIVE

50:35.323 --> 50:37.576
CALLING
APARTMENT 1201

50:38.535 --> 50:42.372
Why the hell are they always out?

50:43.874 --> 50:46.543
Shouldn't they pick up their side dishes?

50:47.294 --> 50:50.130
What am I supposed to do? It's been days.

50:51.715 --> 50:54.009
The entire house reeks of food.

50:59.389 --> 51:00.599
Damn it.

51:08.148 --> 51:09.941
Tae-kyung, give Mom some water.

51:48.605 --> 51:50.065
Where's Ki-jun?

51:50.732 --> 51:52.818
I'm not sure.
I haven't seen him for a while.

51:54.945 --> 51:57.239
Darn it. He should be busy right now.

52:03.829 --> 52:04.996
What should I do?

52:05.997 --> 52:07.249
What should I do?

52:08.375 --> 52:09.793
What will happen?

52:10.794 --> 52:11.962
What should I do?

52:16.383 --> 52:18.760
Ha-kyung, it's me.

52:18.844 --> 52:22.013
I'm sorry, but can you help me this once?

52:22.848 --> 52:24.808
Damn it! Are you crazy?

52:24.891 --> 52:26.810
Don't text her! Don't do it.

52:26.893 --> 52:29.688
Don't do it. You shouldn't.

52:29.771 --> 52:32.357
Then what should I do?

52:32.440 --> 52:33.900
What should I do?

52:33.984 --> 52:35.777
What do you think? You should call her.

52:36.361 --> 52:37.445
Damn it.

52:42.742 --> 52:44.494
Ha-kyung, it's me.

52:44.578 --> 52:47.664
It must have been tiring
to be on night duty.

52:48.999 --> 52:51.334
Actually, I called because…

52:55.881 --> 52:57.632
Save me this once.

52:58.884 --> 53:00.468
I'm truly sorry,

53:01.052 --> 53:05.807
but could you help me just this once?

53:35.545 --> 53:37.923
How is your mother?

53:39.132 --> 53:40.675
She's better.

53:41.676 --> 53:42.802
That's a relief.

53:50.852 --> 53:52.062
I'm sorry.

53:52.145 --> 53:53.521
What for?

53:56.149 --> 53:57.901
My father…

54:01.196 --> 54:02.739
I feel terrible.

54:07.285 --> 54:09.371
I can't even apologize properly.

54:10.288 --> 54:11.581
Did you eat?

54:19.881 --> 54:20.840
Have some.

54:21.883 --> 54:23.969
My mom made it herself.

54:25.261 --> 54:28.139
She always makes this
around this time of the year.

54:29.516 --> 54:30.350
Why?

54:31.810 --> 54:33.853
It was my father's favorite food,

54:34.354 --> 54:36.481
and tomorrow is his death anniversary.

54:52.998 --> 54:55.375
I think Ha-kyung
takes after you in cooking.

54:55.458 --> 54:57.919
She did well despite
all that complaining, right?

54:59.004 --> 55:00.380
Is she coming tomorrow?

55:01.840 --> 55:02.674
What do you think?

55:03.508 --> 55:04.926
Don't hold your breath.

55:05.010 --> 55:06.803
I know you understand her too.

55:12.684 --> 55:13.977
She did a good job.

55:17.564 --> 55:21.359
The day my father died
is one of the memories

55:22.110 --> 55:24.738
I would love to forget.

55:24.821 --> 55:27.198
SEIZED

55:28.533 --> 55:30.118
I'm home.

55:38.126 --> 55:39.252
Mom.

55:51.765 --> 55:53.266
Are you not home?

56:27.550 --> 56:29.761
After his business went under,

56:31.012 --> 56:33.890
he abandoned us and fled.

56:43.358 --> 56:46.111
That's the kind of father I had.

56:47.112 --> 56:48.696
So don't be

56:49.572 --> 56:51.950
in too much pain because of yours.

56:53.827 --> 56:57.497
"Just as a loud noise is created
when a cloud meets another cloud,

56:58.248 --> 57:01.876
I wish I could be bold enough
to shout unconsciously

57:01.960 --> 57:05.088
in this relationship I have with you."

57:23.356 --> 57:24.774
It's tasty.

57:28.069 --> 57:30.655
"Just as a bright light appears

57:30.738 --> 57:32.657
when a cloud suddenly meets another cloud,

57:33.324 --> 57:35.076
I wish being with you

57:35.910 --> 57:38.788
could shed light on the path
I have wandered away from."

57:40.123 --> 57:41.958
Can you promise me something?

57:47.589 --> 57:48.798
What is it?

57:49.924 --> 57:52.010
If you happen to not love me anymore,

57:52.760 --> 57:54.804
let me be the first to know.

57:55.388 --> 57:56.681
If you become swayed,

57:56.764 --> 57:58.850
I want to be the first one to know.

58:02.061 --> 58:05.607
Of course, my heart
will break once you tell me.

58:05.690 --> 58:07.650
But what's even more painful…

58:09.194 --> 58:11.237
is if I'm kept in the dark.

58:14.365 --> 58:15.617
Not like my father.

58:24.667 --> 58:26.252
Not like Han Ki-jun.

58:32.091 --> 58:34.677
Promise me you won't be like them.

58:37.388 --> 58:40.850
"You shine brightly when you tell me
that rain needs to meet another rain

58:42.227 --> 58:43.978
for them

58:45.104 --> 58:46.731
to get drenched."

58:46.814 --> 58:48.358
I promise.

58:50.777 --> 58:51.945
Okay, then.

58:58.493 --> 58:59.911
Let's live together.

59:04.958 --> 59:06.000
THEMED STORY FOR JULY

59:06.084 --> 59:06.918
I'm finished.

59:08.211 --> 59:09.254
Let's see.

59:10.046 --> 59:12.674
Assistant Director Kim's piece wasn't bad.

59:12.757 --> 59:14.259
You can consider his

59:14.342 --> 59:15.635
as well as mine.

59:15.718 --> 59:17.178
Let me know once you decide.

59:17.762 --> 59:18.721
Okay.

59:18.805 --> 59:19.806
Thank you.

59:25.103 --> 59:26.271
Good work.

59:26.354 --> 59:29.065
Please. I should say that to you instead.

59:30.316 --> 59:32.860
When he becomes anxious,

59:32.944 --> 59:34.988
he tends to bother everyone.

59:35.071 --> 59:36.155
Sorry?

59:36.698 --> 59:38.741
I see. It was a good experience for me.

59:38.825 --> 59:41.661
That's it. Experience.
That's what's important.

59:41.744 --> 59:43.496
I love that attitude of yours.

59:43.580 --> 59:47.083
Look at this.
The mighty Han Ki-jun is back.

59:47.166 --> 59:48.793
Let's get this printed right away.

59:48.876 --> 59:51.629
Yes, sir.
I'll send it to them this instant.

59:53.006 --> 59:55.091
I knew you could do it.

01:00:08.938 --> 01:00:11.107
WILL YOU BE LATE?
I THINK SO. YOU CAN GO TO BED FIRST.

01:00:11.190 --> 01:00:13.026
Can I see you for a minute?

01:00:20.867 --> 01:00:22.994
What's up? Aren't you busy at this hour?

01:00:23.786 --> 01:00:25.121
Would you like a beverage?

01:00:26.748 --> 01:00:29.417
Right. Did you register
our marriage yesterday?

01:00:29.500 --> 01:00:31.628
We should hurry if we want to get a loan.

01:00:31.711 --> 01:00:33.463
Our housing contract will end soon.

01:00:34.172 --> 01:00:37.175
Actually, that's why I wanted to talk.

01:00:37.842 --> 01:00:38.926
Okay. What is it?

01:00:40.762 --> 01:00:42.430
Can we push back

01:00:43.473 --> 01:00:45.391
registering our marriage?

01:00:47.852 --> 01:00:48.936
What?

01:00:52.857 --> 01:00:56.027
You want to live together with me?

01:00:56.611 --> 01:00:59.489
Yes. I want to be with you.

01:01:01.199 --> 01:01:03.451
Move in with me.

01:01:08.331 --> 01:01:10.041
What do you mean?

01:01:10.833 --> 01:01:11.793
Hold on.

01:01:12.502 --> 01:01:14.087
What does this mean?

01:01:14.170 --> 01:01:15.963
You want to push it back?

01:01:17.006 --> 01:01:19.509
Why? What's your reason?

01:01:21.594 --> 01:01:23.930
I just want to.

01:02:04.721 --> 01:02:09.350
Today's atmospheric ozone concentration
is expected to be over 0.3ppm per hour.

01:02:09.434 --> 01:02:12.437
The weather is perfectly fine.
What's with the ozone warning?

01:02:12.520 --> 01:02:14.981
Who handled the complaint calls
that came to the Chief Team today?

01:02:15.064 --> 01:02:16.691
I didn't struggle to pass

01:02:16.774 --> 01:02:19.360
the civil service exam
to handle trivial calls like that.

01:02:19.944 --> 01:02:22.613
We are here to do that kind of work.

01:02:23.656 --> 01:02:24.699
Do it if you want to.

01:02:24.782 --> 01:02:26.159
- What?
- Divorce.

01:02:26.242 --> 01:02:29.328
Haven't you heard that they're living
in the night-duty room?

01:02:29.412 --> 01:02:31.289
Did you just say two of them?

01:02:32.373 --> 01:02:33.207
Lee Si-woo--

01:02:34.584 --> 01:02:37.170
She lived with someone from the KMA?

01:02:38.546 --> 01:02:42.550
I think your husband found out
that you and I lived together.

01:02:43.301 --> 01:02:48.222
Subtitle translation by: Soo-ji Kim
